# 6. Uniform theorem under bounded observation dynamic range

For an ex-ante history-uniform bound, assume each realized likelihood vector obeys

\[
\frac{\max_j g_s(j)}{\min_j g_s(j)}
\le
R
<\infty.
\]

Let

\[
L=\gamma(T),
\qquad
\Delta_L=\Delta(T^L).
\]

For a length-\(L\) block, define

\[
m_s=\min_j g_s(j),
\qquad
M_s=\max_j g_s(j).
\]

Every block entry satisfies

\[
\left(\prod_{s=1}^L m_s\right)
(T^L)_{ij}
\le
(A_b)_{ij}
\le
\left(\prod_{s=1}^L M_s\right)
(T^L)_{ij}.
\]

Hence every projective cross-ratio is bounded by the corresponding cross-ratio of \(T^L\) times

\[
\left(
\prod_{s=1}^L
\frac{M_s}{m_s}
\right)^2.
\]

Therefore

\[
\boxed{
\Delta(A_b)
\le
\Delta_L
+
2\sum_{s=1}^L
\log\frac{M_s}{m_s}.
}
\]

Under the uniform dynamic-range bound,

\[
\boxed{
\Delta(A_b)
\le
\bar\Delta_L
:=
\Delta(T^L)+2L\log R.
}
\]

Define

\[
\boxed{
\bar\tau_L
=
\tanh\left(\frac{\bar\Delta_L}{4}\right)
<1.
}
\]

---

# 7. Uniform sparse-transition pathwise horizon

### Theorem CW-002C.3 — Primitive-block history-uniform forgetting

For every positive-likelihood observation history and every

\[
n\ge L,
\qquad
q=\left\lfloor\frac nL\right\rfloor,
\]

\[
\boxed{
d_H(
\pi_n^{x,h},
\pi_n^{x',h}
)
\le
\bar\Delta_L
\bar\tau_L^{q-1}.
}
\]

Consequently,

\[
\boxed{
r(E_{n,h})
\le
\left(1-\frac1m\right)
\tanh
\left[
\frac{
\bar\Delta_L
\bar\tau_L^{q-1}
}{4}
\right]
\qquad
\forall h.
}
\]

Thus one-step positivity is unnecessary.

Primitive support plus bounded positive observation dynamic range suffices for a deterministic pathwise Le Cam horizon.

